abstract = {The rapid development of technology has led to a shift in the field of language teaching from traditional classroom instruction to the use of interactive technologies. This article reviews various interactive technological tools, including mobile applications, online course platforms, and the application and benefits of virtual reality (VR), augmented reality (AR), and artificial intelligence in language teaching and learning. Despite the many positive effects brought about by interactive technology, there are also challenges, including issues of technological accessibility, control over teaching content and quality, and the need for teacher training in the integration of technology. Additionally, the article analyzes the direction of future development.},
